A working press. A sheet sent into the world. Words that become part of a lif=
e.

Our new one-minute film brings together the presses in our Austin shop, the s=
tory of the first printed Declaration, and the Western Canon. The machinery i=
s ours. The historical scenes are contemporary reconstructions. The invitatio=
n is simple: read the words, keep the source, and give the enduring a place i=
n your room.

Watch History has a pulse. Then explore the broadsides behind the story.

